VDR Plugin 'drmdevice' Revision History
---------------------------------------

drmdevice is the continuation of softhddevice-drm-gles. For the changes up to
softhddevice-drm-gles 1.7.3 see the git history of
https://github.com/rellla/vdr-plugin-softhddevice-drm-gles

2026-10-12: Version 2.0.0

- Renamed the plugin from softhddevice-drm-gles to drmdevice. The functionality
  is identical to softhddevice-drm-gles 1.7.3.
- The plugin is now loaded with -P drmdevice, the setup.conf entries are named
  drmdevice.*, the SVDRP commands are sent with PLUG drmdevice and the key
  macros use @drmdevice. Existing configurations have to be adapted.
- Renamed the source files and classes (e.g. softhddevice.cpp -> device.cpp).

2026-10-20: Version 2.0.1

- Started the playback nearly at the end of the a/v-sync corridor and increased
  the size of the drm queue (fixes frame drops with some HD live streams on the
  Raspberry Pi 4).
- Fixed the detection of video buffer underruns (underruns on 576i channels).
- Fixed crashes with corrupted streams (e.g. bad reception) in the PES
  reassembly and in the H.264 parser (endless loop, wrong height, RBSP length).
- Fixed crashes in detached state, e.g. at VDR shutdown, if VDR was started
  detached (-D) or detached via SVDRP or the plugin menu.
- Fixed deadlocks, if the pip stream is torn down on a detach.
- Fixed crashes, memory and resource leaks in the menu, the mediaplayer, the
  video stream, the audio filter graph, the drm device, the OpenGL/ES OSD and
  the device tree parsing.
- Fixed buffer overflows in the software render paths.
- Fixed the pixel format fallback and the extradata handling of the video
  decoder.
- Fixed the hardware mixer volume for mixer elements with a large volume range
  and the soft volume on partial writes.
- Skip the audio channel mapping, if ALSA reports unknown channel positions.
- Fixed the command line and SVDRP handling: -w is also accepted without
  OpenGL/ES support, -x is listed in the help text, the SVDRP help lists PIPP
  and PLAY needs an url and an attached plugin.
- Fixed the default minimum mastering luminance of the HDR metadata
  (0.005 cd/m^2 instead of 0.004 cd/m^2).
- Only the main stream changes the display mode, the pip stream doesn't anymore.
- Don't lose video packets, if the packet queue is full (end of a recording,
  still pictures).
- Send IEC 61937 pause bursts instead of NULL data bursts while paused in
  passthrough mode.
- FFmpeg messages are filtered by their log level now. Added the setup option
  "FFmpeg log level" (LogFFmpegLevel) to raise the level of the FFmpeg debug
  logs to verbose, debug or trace.
- Fixed the build against VDR 2.4 and link all used FFmpeg libraries
  explicitly.
- Fixed many compiler and cppcheck warnings, removed unused code.
- Added unit tests and regression tests for the fixed bugs, the CI builds with
  gcc and clang against several VDR versions and runs the tests.

2026-10-20: Version 2.0.2

- Fixed the detection of AC-3 streams with bsid 10, which were treated as
  E-AC-3.
- Reopen the audio decoder, if the audio codec changes within the same PES
  stream id (e.g. a switch between an AC-3 and an E-AC-3 track).
- Always drop the ALSA PCM before changing the hw params (silent audio after a
  change from E-AC-3 to AC-3 in passthrough mode).
- Require the exact sample rate and channel count for the passthrough and
  decode the audio, if the device doesn't offer them (e.g. E-AC-3 needs
  192kHz).
- With the "auto append AES" option, the IEC 958 channel status is set
  according to the current format (non-audio flag and sample rate) instead of
  once at startup.

2026-10-20: Version 2.0.3

- Fixed the doxygen configuration and all doxygen warnings, complemented the
  source documentation. The CI fails on new doxygen warnings.
- The source documentation is always rebuilt with make srcdoc.

2026-10-23: Version 2.0.4

- Mediaplayer: a media file is replayed like a VDR recording. The play modes
  (play, pause, fast and slow motion forward and backward), the trick speeds,
  the keys (incl. Setup.SkipSeconds, Setup.MultiSpeedMode and the time search)
  and the replay display (mode, remaining time) work like VDR's replay
  control. Prev/Next play the previous/next title of a playlist, Back opens
  the file menu with the played file selected. The keys are documented in the
  README.
- Mediaplayer: the replay of a local file continues at the position, where
  it was stopped (backed up by 10s). The positions of the last 100 files are
  stored in the file "resume" in the plugin's cache directory.
- Mediaplayer: all packets are sent in the 90kHz timebase of VDR (fixes the
  a/v sync and the trick speeds of other containers than MPEG-TS).
- Mediaplayer: the cover art of an audio file isn't taken as video stream.
- Mediaplayer: the random play is seeded only once (titles, which started
  within the same second, got the same random number).
- Mediaplayer: the playlist menu is updated by the main thread (the osd isn't
  thread safe).

2026-10-23: Version 2.0.5

- Added TrueHD passthrough (AudioPassthrough bit 32) and DTS-HD passthrough
  (Master Audio and High Resolution Audio, AudioPassthrough bit 64). TrueHD
  and DTS-HD Master Audio need a device with 8 channels and 192kHz (HDMI).
  DTS-HD is only recognized by the mediaplayer, otherwise the DTS core is
  passed through.
- A bitstream is sent with the sample rate of the stream (e.g. 44.1kHz from
  the mediaplayer), E-AC-3 with four times the rate.
- The automatic AES parameters (IEC 60958 channel status) are enabled by
  default. The option is replaced by "Disable automatic AES"
  (AudioDisableAutoAES). A device, which doesn't accept AES parameters, is
  used without them.
- The spdif bursts are kept intact: audio is dropped in complete bursts, a
  burst gets the pts of its first packet, a flush resets the spdif muxer.
- A muted bitstream is replaced by pause bursts instead of zeros, so the
  receiver keeps the sync.
- A failed passthrough is tried again with every channel switch and replay
  start (e.g. the receiver was switched on meanwhile).
- Fixed the DTS frame size check and the reassembly of DTS and AAC frames,
  the DTS-HD extension substream is kept with its core frame.
- Unit tests with real audio streams of all codecs.

2026-10-23: Version 2.0.6

- Fixed a hang, if a skin stored an image while detached (the OpenGL thread
  waited endlessly for the renderer). The image cache is cleaned up with the
  OpenGL thread.
- The EGL surface, context and display are freed with the renderer (they
  leaked with every detach/attach).
- After a detach or attach by SVDRP an open menu is closed, so the next menu
  key opens the menu again.
- The hotkeys of the plugin menu (key macros) are only accepted in the main
  menu, the color keys of the mediaplayer menus work again.
- The clock drift correction isn't reset at its output limit anymore.
- Fixed a data race of the log string helpers and an overflow of the osd
  colors of a screenshot.
- README: fixed the name of the AudioNormalize setup entry.

2026-10-25: Version 2.1.0

- Zoom levels to crop black bars of the broadcast (ZoomLevel1-5). The zoom is
  selected in the plugin menu, with the key macros "@drmdevice Green 1/2",
  with SVDRP ZOOM or with the Blue key in the mediaplayer.
- Automatic audio passthrough with the codecs, which the HDMI sink reports in
  its ELD (AudioPassthrough bit 128). The passthrough can be switched on and
  off in the plugin menu, with the key macro "@drmdevice Yellow 1" and with
  SVDRP PASS (not stored).
- Mediaplayer: the audio track can be selected (Audio key), text subtitles
  (SubRip, ASS/SSA, mov_text) are shown (Subtitles key), files and folders
  in the video directory can be deleted in the file menu (Blue key, not a
  recording, which is recorded or replayed), HLS streams are played.
- Output for the dvd plugin: the DVD audio (AC-3, DTS, LPCM) is played, AC-3
  and DTS can be passed through.
- The setup menu lists its sections, OK opens a section. In a section, OK
  stores the settings and Back discards the changes.
- The setup menu shows the played video and audio stream, the display mode,
  the audio output and the passthrough state in the statistics, which are
  updated every second.
- SVDRP PION shows the given channel (number, channel ID or name) in the
  pip window.
- The SVDRP commands reply with the codes of VDR's commands (501 invalid
  argument, 550 not executed, 554 failed).
- Passthrough: a gap of the bitstream is bridged with pause bursts and an
  underrun resyncs audio and video, the ringbuffer isn't dropped after a
  failed write anymore (the receiver lost the lock and the audio fell out).
- Passthrough: the audio device is started, when a bitstream nearly filled
  its buffer (every start was delayed by 150ms and logged an error).
- The playback starts with the buffered data, if a player waits for empty
  buffers (fixes a hang of the dvd plugin before a still picture).
- An audio codec, which can't be decoded, is dropped instead of aborting
  VDR. The audio decoder of the mediaplayer leaked with every file.
- Pip: the pip functions are serialized, a pip window without a channel is
  closed, a channel without video isn't shown.
- Pip: fixed crashes with SVDRP pip commands during a detach, with an
  external player in detached state and with a deleted pip channel. The pip
  channel is only used with the channels lock.
